// rsi-round-run.bml — Terminal-RSI's rounds over the native-turn queue (form-stdlib/bml/rsi-rounds.bml).
//   printf '{"rounds":3,"home":".hearth/session-learning","learn":1}' | ./fkwu observe/rsi-round-run.bml
// stdin, one JSON line, every key optional:
//   run             the run's id (default rsi-<unix ms>); a run named again inherits its critic
//   rounds          train rounds (default 2): eval, then train, for each, then one eval more
//   queue           the gap queue (default learn/native-turn-queue.jsonl); gaps (first n of it, 0 for all)
//   held_out_every  one hash bucket in this many is held out (default 4)
//   turn_ms         each turn's wall deadline (default 900000); turn_door (default observe/native-turn-run.bml)
//   calib_steps     critic-only updates before advantages are used (default 4); critic_lr_milli (default 500)
//   home            the session-learning home the lessons are offered to (unnamed: no lesson is offered)
//   learn           1 drains the learner between rounds (default 0)
//   receipts, work  where round rows land (receipts/rsi-rounds.jsonl) and the run's ledgers stay (.hearth/rsi)
// Prints the run line, then one JSON row per phase as it lands. Exit 0; a turn that exited nonzero is counted, not hidden.
// preflight-exec: forbidden
import form-stdlib/bml/rsi-rounds.bml;
section [form.bml] {
 rsi-run(dop-doc(rsi-door(), stdin-text(), rsi-spec()));
 0;
}
